ighlands, and is the region's commercial and administrative centre. It's an agreeable Victorian town that has no stand-out tourist attractions of its own, but has good transport and choice of lodging and eating places. So it's a good base for exploring the nearby Loch Ness, Black Isle, Culloden, Spey Valley and Cairngorms National Park.","grounding":[{"source":"wikivoyage","title":"Inverness","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Inverness","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"short":"Inverness is a city in Scotland, gateway to the Highlands. Inverness Castle and Culloden Battlefield make up most of six hours of touring, and Inverness Cathedral with Eden Court sit nearby, June through August is the season.","short_src":"rewrite","facts":{"population":47790,"visit_h":4.3}},"highlights":[{"id":"hl-inverness-cathedral","name":"Inverness Cathedral","kind":"Cathedral","lat":57.47444,"lon":-4.22917,"dist_km":0.5,"rank_score":8.93,"resolved_by":"catalogue","image":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Inverness_Cathedral.jpg/960px-Inverness_Cathedral.jpg","author":"Lucas Kendall","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licence_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Inverness_Cathedral.jpg","ok_print":true}},{"id":"hl-inverness-castle","name":"Inverness Castle","kind":"Castle","lat":57.47631,"lon":-4.2255,"dist_km":0.3,"rank_score":8.72,"resolved_by":"catalogue","image":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Inverness_Castle%2C_Scotland_-_Diliff.jpg/960px-Inverness_Castle%2C_Scotland_-_Diliff.jpg","author":"Diliff","licence":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licence_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Inverness_Castle,_Scotland_-_Diliff.jpg","w":5000,"h":3452,"ok_print":true}},{"id":"hl-caledonian-stadium","name":"Caledonian Stadium","kind":"Landmark","lat":57.49472,"lon":-4.2175,"dist_km":1.8,"rank_score":7.61,"resolved_by":"catalog